    "provenance": "Generated 2026-10-21 from the vendor hub.aulacn.com driver bundle: geometry + keyValue from the F75 layout array `t` (80 keys; info-Ce0byjrM.js initDeviceLayout selects `t` for PID 10025 = 0x2729) and names/HID usages from master key map `y` in docs/context/issue-6-mini60-pro-raw/driver_src/HFD-D07mGRx8.js -- the same method that produced the hardware-verified aula-mini60he-pro.json. Names follow the existing layouts' code->name convention.",
    "note": "index = the firmware keyValue (stride-16 matrix shared with the MINI 60 HE PRO: Esc=0, F1-F12 = 1-12, number row 16-28 + Backspace 92, Tab row 32-44 + Backslash 60, Caps row 48-59 + Enter 76, Shift row 64-75, bottom row 80-91; nav column Del 106 / PgUp 105 / PgDn 108 / End 107). The rotary knob is not part of the vendor layout and is not modelled. hidCode 0xfa for Fn is the Aether convention. KNOWN GAPS: the firmware key table holds usage 0xAF in the Fn slot (85), and its F1-F12 base records (1-12) are empty (firmware default); the table also populates 30 slots outside this layout (shared full-size defaults such as the numpad) which are deliberately not drawn. tests/test_f75.py pins all of this against the contributor read-back."
